Subject: [PATCH 10/11] clk: qcom: add voltage-corner and debug support

Port regulator-backed voltage-corner votes to the target's common-clock and
regulator APIs, retaining per-level aggregation, transactional rollback, and
the temporary maximum-level proxy vote until CCF sync_state. Adapt selected
PLL and RCG operations to the target's pre/post-rate hooks and return setup
errors instead of silently ignoring failed register writes. Add a checked
register-update sequence helper and preserve qcom,critical-devices consumers
as enabled clock references, including the topaz QUP clock dependency.

Add the Khaje debug-mux measurement support used by the debug clock driver.
All selector values in the Khaje data are treated as valid (no sentinel); the
debugfs parent-change path rejects a missing/unresolved parent before calling
clk_set_parent. No voltage vote is removed by this patch.

This patch has not been compiled or validated on hardware.

